# Cases the reference compiler cannot compile (PROPOSAL.md §1b, harness/README.md):
# the reference side skips them, and each has only a .iecf.trace, checked by hand.
connections   # program connections: iec2c crashes or writes C that does not compile
sfc
parts         # CONCAT_DATE, CONCAT_TOD, CONCAT_DT, the SPLITs: the reference compiler has none of Table 36's
splitwrap     # the same: SPLIT
splitindex
splitclamp
splitenable
ldates        # LDATE, LTOD, LDT: the reference compiler has none
fbskip        # NOT ENO => : the reference compiler's iec2c fails (internal compiler error)
progio        # program connections, as connections
located       # an LTIME at an address: the reference compiler refuses it, and its TIME is a structure
locdata       # an array at an address: the reference compiler refuses it
refimage      # REF_TO: r^ := ... does not compile in the reference compiler's C; REF_TO a block crashes it
refto         # REFERENCE TO: CODESYS's, an extension (docs/extensions.md); the reference compiler has none
widen         # implicit conversions (Ed.3 6.6.1.6): the reference compiler has none (Ed.2)
fnoutx        # a FUNCTION's outputs: NOT q => crashes the reference compiler, no implicit conversions, an output into an element does not compile
fnorder       # VAR_EXTERNAL in a FUNCTION: the reference compiler (Ed.2) refuses it
chars         # CHAR is Ed.3's: the reference compiler (Ed.2) has none
implicit      # the implicit-externals extension: the reference compiler has none
namespaces    # NAMESPACE (Ed.3): the reference compiler (Ed.2) has none; two files
globalns      # the global-namespace extension, and namespaces
inoutcopy     # an in-out given an array element: the reference compiler's C does not compile (assignment to expression with array type)
fneffen       # EN on a FUNCTION with effects: VAR_EXTERNAL in a FUNCTION, which the reference compiler (Ed.2) refuses
stringchars   # s[i], a STRING's character (Ed.3): the reference compiler (Ed.2) has none
wstrings      # WCHAR and s[i] (Ed.3): the reference compiler (Ed.2) has neither
wlocated      # a WSTRING at an address: WCHAR and s[i] (Ed.3), and the reference compiler refuses an array there
